From e6c236960e956f420926b06e3357997592a4aa89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OneFeiFan <3022504358@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 05:41:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] zram: add Xiaomi ExtM (memory extension) support
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Bring the zram driver to Xiaomi's ExtM implementation, so HyperOS's
memory extension (PerfInit + the ExtM service) works on the built-in
zram: batched writeback ("idle <wb_max> <wb_idle_min>"), idle aging by
time (time_list, idle_stat), low-compression-ratio-first writeback
(low_compress_ratio), page lifetime and size statistics (pages_life,
avg_size, new, new_stat, origin_pages_max, wb_pages_max) and SIGUSR1 to
stop a running writeback. The new statistics are behind
CONFIG_MIUI_ZRAM_MEMORY_TRACKING, enabled in gki_defconfig here.

zram_drv.c and zram_drv.h are taken from Xiaomi's GPL kernel source; it
is ACK-based and already carries every ACK change our 5.10.272 zram has
(filp_open_block, page_index writeback, the zero-size backing device
check). Local changes on top: the default compressor stays
CONFIG_ZRAM_DEF_COMP (0016), and old-style empty parameter lists get
"void" so it builds with -Werror=strict-prototypes on newer clang.
Kconfig is a clean three-way merge of ours and Xiaomi's.

Not included: the memory-freeze part (mfz_enable, mfz_disk_quota,
mfz_compr_data_size, mfz_idle_stat), which Xiaomi only publishes in its
6.6 trees, and writeback_quota / zgroup_enable, which no public source
has. PerfInit logs those as missing and carries on.

Origin: MiCode/Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource spinel-v-oss 49ff345d71ab (5.10.233), drivers/block/zram/{zram_drv.c,zram_drv.h,Kconfig}
Upstream-Status: Not-Applicable（小米厂商实现）
KABI: none（zram 内建，改动限于 drivers/block/zram 内部）
Depends-On: 0016 内建 zram，0017 ZRAM_WRITEBACK
Notes: 小米 yudi-t-oss（5.10.160）的 zram 是原版，没有 ExtM，因此取 spinel；内存冻结（mfz）在小米 6.6 源码（bixi-v-oss）里，未移植
Tested-On: 本地 clang 18.1.3 交叉编译 drivers/block/zram 通过（aarch64，gki_defconfig）；未实机验证

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
